### Quick Start Example 1: Health Check
# Test if the server is running (no authentication needed)
GET http://localhost:8080/health

###

### Quick Start Example 2: Get Video Info
# Title, duration and the available formats of a YouTube video
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/video/info?youtubeUrl=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ
# Add your credentials if Basic Auth is enabled:
# Authorization: Basic your-username your-password

###

### Quick Start Example 3: Create a Clip
# Create a 10-second clip
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/clip
Content-Type: application/json
# Add your credentials if Basic Auth is enabled:
# Authorization: Basic your-username your-password

{
  "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ",
  "from": "00:00:10",
  "to": "00:00:20",
  "preset": "video"
}

# Copy the job ID from the response for the next steps

###

### Quick Start Example 4: Check Job Status
# Replace "your-job-id-here" with the actual job ID from step 3
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/jobs/your-job-id-here
# Add your credentials if Basic Auth is enabled:
# Authorization: Basic your-username your-password

# Keep running this until "status" is "completed" (or "error")

###

### Quick Start Example 5: Download the Clip
# Replace "your-job-id-here" with the actual job ID from step 3
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/clip?jobId=your-job-id-here
# Add your credentials if Basic Auth is enabled:
# Authorization: Basic your-username your-password

# This will download the completed video clip

###